From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Toon Verwaest <verwaest@chromium.org>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 14:10:48 +0200
Subject: [interpreter] Initialize private accessors early in BuildClassLiteral
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Private accessors were previously initialized after evaluating the
extends clause and computed property keys. If execution was suspended or
escaped during computed property key evaluation (e.g. via a generator
yield), the private accessor context slots could be observed in their
uninitialized state (the_hole) and cached as constants by Maglev.

Initialize private accessor pairs early alongside private methods and
brand symbols, before evaluating the extends clause or computed property
keys.

TAG=agy
CONV=1b7d9654-2731-4157-8abc-cd9414138332
Fixed: 559932543

Change-Id: I3bb6cb9a92513249c225963be85a0ca9acc0286b
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/v8/v8/+/8424799
Reviewed-by: Marja Hölttä <marja@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Toon Verwaest <verwaest@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#109928}

diff --git a/src/interpreter/bytecode-generator.cc b/src/interpreter/bytecode-generator.cc
